ADC AND TEMPERATURE SENSOR WORKFLOW

The RP2040 provides an onboard temperature sensor. PicoNIX maps
it to a device and also exposes get_temperature via MCP.

PREFERRED AGENT PATH
  get_temperature()       MCP direct sensor reading
  pins                    see mapped input/peripheral pins
  ls /dev/adc

RAW DEVICE
  /dev/adc/temp          sensor-facing virtual device
  hexdump /dev/adc/temp 0 4
Raw bytes are not automatically a text decimal temperature.
Use the published device encoding before interpreting output.

WHAT IS SAFE
  Reading onboard temperature is non-destructive and makes a
  good MCP introductory exercise. Repeated rapid polling still
  uses CPU and consumes connection bandwidth.

WHAT NEEDS CHECKING
  Other ADC inputs require correct electrical wiring and voltage
  range. Do not connect or sample unknown high-voltage sources.
  If a device is not listed under /dev/adc, do not invent a path.

FOR AUTOMATED TESTS
  Call get_temperature twice separated by a short interval.
  Confirm both calls return, then compare only broad plausibility.
  Do not infer precise physical room temperature from the CPU die
  sensor; it measures chip temperature under load.
